---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy notice"
  description="How Drimini handles information submitted through its project enquiry form."
  bodyClass="privacy-page"
>
  <article class="legal-page shell">
    <header>
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy notice</p>
      <h1>What happens to your enquiry.</h1>
      <p class="legal-page__updated">Last updated: 2 October 2026</p>
    </header>

    <section>
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        The project enquiry form asks for your name, work email, company, and a
        description of the work. Your role, approximate timeline, and approximate
        budget are optional. Spam protection also processes limited technical
        information about the submission.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Why we use it</h2>
      <p>
        Drimini uses this information to understand your request, decide whether
        the work may be a fit, reply to you, and protect the form from abuse. We do
        not use enquiry details for unrelated marketing or sell them.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Where it goes</h2>
      <p>
        Cloudflare processes the form, performs spam verification, and stores the
        enquiry in a Drimini database hosted on Cloudflare D1. Drimini reviews
        enquiries through Cloudflare's authenticated dashboard or an authenticated
        local Wrangler session. If Drimini replies, the resulting email
        conversation is handled through VK WorkSpace.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Enquiries are kept only while we need them to respond, evaluate the
        potential work, maintain the resulting business conversation, or meet an
        applicable legal obligation. Enquiries that are no longer needed are
        permanently deleted from D1. Archiving an enquiry is an organizational
        step and does not delete it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask Drimini to correct or delete an enquiry by emailing
        contact@drimini.com, or by using the contact form and writing “Privacy
        request” at the start of the project field. Your rights may vary with your
        location and any applicable law.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Keep sensitive material out</h2>
      <p>
        Do not submit passwords, access tokens, production credentials, regulated
        data, or other sensitive information. We can arrange an appropriate
        channel later if a conversation requires it.
      </p>
    </section>

    <a class="text-link" href="/contact">Return to contact <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
